<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( Formalized ESG governance & policy book. Kia now publishes an ESG Policy Book and has set board-level oversight and a double materiality assessment that informs its targets. Disclosure granularity. Public disclosures are improving year-on-year, but investors seeking fully granular, region-level Scope 3 line items or supplier audit scores may find gaps \(Kia is closing those gaps via phased reporting updates\). Shareholder structure / strategic backing. Hyundai Motor Group is the largest shareholder \(roughly ~34%\), giving Kia scale benefits, shared platforms and stronger governance linkages)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [12 13]
>>
