419 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (DuPont Summary Net Profit Margin has seen a drastic increase from 2020 to 2021, post-pandemic recovery. Ever since, it has seen a gradual increase, going from 6.81% to 9.1%, hinting at the faster rate of increase of the net income as compared to the revenue. This is likely due to the effective partnership with Hyundai Motors for shared supplier procurement. Asset Turnover Ratio has been consistent over the period, signifying that there has been a good utilisation of assets in generating revenue. The rising margins are the main driver - Kia is earning more per unit sold due to SUVs and Sonet models \(Premium Positioning being responsible for this\). Also, operational efficiency is strong as indicated by a consistent Asset Turnover ratio. This contributes to an increase in the ROE.)
/E (DuPont Summary Net Profit Margin has seen a drastic increase from 2020 to 2021, post-pandemic recovery. Ever since, it has seen a gradual increase, going from 6.81% to 9.1%, hinting at the faster rate of increase of the net income as compared to the revenue. This is likely due to the effective partnership with Hyundai Motors for shared supplier procurement. Asset Turnover Ratio has been consistent over the period, signifying that there has been a good utilisation of assets in generating revenue. The rising margins are the main driver - Kia is earning more per unit sold due to SUVs and Sonet models \(Premium Positioning being responsible for this\). Also, operational efficiency is strong as indicated by a consistent Asset Turnover ratio. This contributes to an increase in the ROE.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
